review:
Lots of useful bits of info here for the new user or even an experienced user.  I came away with lots of shortcuts and bits of info that I didn't know.  Some basic keyboard shortcuts, for example, are covered in this course.  One I really liked is the "Dock to Desktop" key (ctrl-alt-d) which opens a notepad-like page on the right side of the screen.  It's a quick and easy way to take notes while viewing something else.  Pressing the Windows+N keys opens up a Quick Note is another shortcut.

Some other nuggets:
[list]
[*]Sections can be password protected;
[*]OneNote can convert handwriting to text or math equations;
[*]Audio and video clips can be searched for words or phrases;
[*]Pages can have sub-pages;
[*]Tags can be applied to whole notes, words or phrases within a note, drawings, pictures, or attached files;
[*]Pages can be annotated or marked up using a ton of built-in tools - pen, highlighter, colors, and more;
[*]Notebooks can have templates to apply a pre-defined style to a notebook; and 
[*]Notebooks, Sections, or Pages can be exported to OneNote, Word, PDF, XPS, or Single File Web Pages.
[/list]

The narrator is the same from the other Professor Teaches courses.  He's easy on the ears and easy to follow.

The course is interactive so you get to move around in OneNote and complete tasks.  Not just a boring lecture.  You are hands-on in this course!

This is a great course for those new to OneNote or looking for some tips to become more productive.

What should I start with? I am still grieving as the ending credits are rolling. The music accompanying it makes my grief even more punctuated. I've learned that the choices we don't pay much attention to affect the lives of other people.

The game tells you that you will need pen, paper and a calculator in order to progress, because many hints are hidden inside audios that you need to listen to very carefully in order to understand the story. 

Sincerely, when I got to the climax scene, I have learned something terrible. The car crash was no accident...

PROS:
- Great RPG;
- Atmospheric music;
- Saving is my life!!
- Character sprite cute and well-executed;
- Story built up nicely;
- Easy to obtain achievements;
- No monster! Thank Heaven!

CONS:
- I had to turn the volume up to hear the spirit crystals audio;
- Even if it has Steam Overlay, I couldn't take any screenshot.

To conclude, I recommend it to anyone who would like a scary story. It might disappoint some children of today because it lacks corpses, monsters and the like, but in my humble opinion this is what makes a good game: the story, the atmosphere, the macabre hints, the music, the player's epiphany after the climax.

This game is one of the most fun and challenging vr games I've seen since superhot. With Loneliness has the most enjoyable gameplay mechanics, and is 100% worth its price, why isn't this game already flooding the vr scenes?

10000/10


PS: Watch your roof, mine was punched a couple times ;~;

This does bring back the memories, even if it is fan-made.
There are three minigames:
1. Memory match: you don't need me to tell you how to play it, just make pairs;
2. Fashion Frenzy: guessing game about choosing accessories on a character;
3. Cake Factory: the GREATEST OF ALL TIME, the minigame that everyone remembers.
And that's all!
Back in the day this simplicity is all that we needed, and it is a real shame that the real one does not longer come with windows anymore, forcing you to go on sketchy websites only to satisfy your nostalgia.
It's not the same game, since some things like the goofy sounds are missing, but it still was great to remember such a great time in my life.

Now for the achievements:
Enter the game for free achievement.
1. Memory Match: Win on easy, medium and hard, win on hard with no tips, get 10 joker, mixer and chef cards, and use tips 10 times (start on easy, use it, restart);
2. Fashion Frenzy: Win on easy, medium and hard, then try getting all 5 accessories right on the first attempt (takes a long time, but try using repeated colors once or twice. This has shortened the grind from hours to a few tries);
3. Cake Factory: Bake a total of 300 cakes (farm on easy), play on hard to use a few toppings 10 times each, get the Valentine's cake and win on hard;
THEN, lose to time in Memory Match for two more. Yep, the hardest achievement is to lose.

DarK City: Vienna is a detective Hidden Object story that is good to play if you're a fan of the HO series. You start by investigating the mystery regarding a masked figure (a direct inspiration from the Phantom of the Opera) and a mystical disappearing muse in the bonus chapter. 

PROS:
- Male protagonist!
- Good graphics;
- Good music;
- Journal entries;
- Fast travelling map;
- Varied hidden object games;
- Bundle of extras good to try;
- So many good mini-games;
- Two sets of collectibles that you can spot easily;
- Feels like Charles Dickens' novels mixed with the Phantom of the Opera and any detective story.

NEUTRE:
- It does not give the masked figure's sidekick's point of view.
- The masked figurine isn't a vampire, though he looks like one. :)

CONS:
- The story could be improved;
- A little bit of mystery and imprevisibility wouldn't hurt;
- Voice acting could be better, but it's good as it is;
- Some subtitles don't appear in the male detective's deductions.

Over all, it has been great fun to play this game. Opera houses, competitivity between artists, secrets, love triangles, orphans, opera singers, mystical swami, masked entities, you name it. It was fun and informative.

